                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative quantum field theory
            the construction of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering+matrix"} scattering matrix
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interacting+field+algebra+of+observables"} interacting field algebra of observables
            for a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interaction"} interaction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi int
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g S_{int}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbation+theory"} perturbing
            around a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field+theory"} free field
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum"} vacuum
            %em normalization
            of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/time-ordered+products"} time-ordered products
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+diagrams"} Feynman diagrams
            (traditionally called
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} "re"-normalizations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interactions"} interactions
            that appear where several of the original interaction vertices defined by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi int
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g S_{int}
            coincide.
          %p
            Whenever a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi RG
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} RG
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} acts
            on the space of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observables"} observables
            of the theory such that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugation"} conjugation
            by this action takes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization+scheme"} ("re"-)normalization schemes
            into each other, then these choices of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} ("re"-)normalization
            are parameterized by – or “flow with” – the elements of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi RG
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} RG
            %em renormalization group flow
            (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FlowRenormalizationGroup"}
            below); often called
            = succeed "," do
              %em RG flow
          %p
            The archetypical example here is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi RG
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} RG
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scaling+transformations"} scaling transformations
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ScalingTransformations"}
            below), which induces a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization+group+flow"} renormalization group flow
            (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RGFlowScalingTransformations"}
            below) due to the particular nature of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wightman+propagator"} Wightman propagator
            resp.
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+propagator"} Feynman propagator
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            (example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ScalarFieldMassDimensionOnMinkowskiSpacetime"}
            below). In this case the choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} ("re"-)normalization
            hence “flows with scale”.
          %p
            Now the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/main+theorem+of+perturbative+renormalization"} main theorem of perturbative renormalization
              states that (if only the basic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization+condition"} renormalization condition
              called “field independence” is satisfied) any two choices of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization+scheme"} ("re"-)normalization schemes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}'
              are related by a unique
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interaction+vertex+redefinition"} interaction vertex redefinition
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒵
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{Z}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mo ′
                  %mo =
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi 𝒵
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{S}' = \mathcal{S} \circ \mathcal{Z}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Applied to a parameterization/flow of renormalization choices by a group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi RG
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} RG
            this hence induces an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interaction+vertex+redefinition"} interaction vertex redefinition
            as a function of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi RG
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} RG
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adiabatic+switching"} adiabatically switched
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coupling+constants"} coupling constants
            as changing under such an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interaction+vertex+redefinition"} interaction vertex redefinition
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coupling+constants"} coupling constants
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_j
            that are parameterized by elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi RG
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} RG
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi 𝒵
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ρ
                        %mi vac
                    %mi ρ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{Z}_{\rho_{vac}}^\rho
                  \\;\colon\;
                  \\{g_j\}
                  \\mapsto
                  \\{g_j(\rho)\}
          %p
            This dependendence is called
            %em running of the coupling constants
            under the renormalization group flow (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CouplingRunning"}
            below).
          %p
            One example of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization+group+flow"} renormalization group flow
            is that induced by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scaling+transformations"} scaling transformations
            (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RGFlowScalingTransformations"}
            below). This is the original and main example of the concept (
            %a{:href => "#GellMannLow54"}> Gell-Mann &amp; Low 54
            )
          %p
            In this case the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/running+of+the+coupling+constants"} running of the coupling constants
            may be understood as expressing how “more”
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interactions"} interactions
            (at higher energy/shorter
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wavelength"} wavelength
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_j(\rho)
            on the parameter
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            happens to be
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+function"} differentiable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logarithm"} logarithmic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivative"} derivative
            (denoted “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ψ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
            ” in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#GellMannLow54"} Gell-Mann &amp; Low 54
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/beta+function"} beta function
            (
            %a{:href => "#Callan70"}> Callan 70
            ,
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#Symanzik70"} Symanzik 70
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi ρ
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∂
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mi j
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi ρ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\beta(g) \coloneqq \rho \frac{\partial g_j}{\partial \rho}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Notice that this is related to, but conceptually different from,
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Polchinski%27s+flow+equation"} Polchinski's flow equation
            in the context of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilsonian+RG"} Wilsonian RG
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/running+of+the+coupling+constants"} running of the coupling constants
            is not quite a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization+group+flow"} renormalization group flow
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cocycle"} group 1-cocycle
            (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CocycleRunningCoupling"}
            below). For the case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scaling+transformations"} scaling transformations
            this may be called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gell-Mann-Low+renormalization+cocycle"} Gell-Mann-Low renormalization cocycle
            (
            %a{:href => "#BrunettiDuetschFredenhagen09"}> Brunetti-Dütsch-Fredenhagen 09
            ).
          %p For more see at
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+A+first+idea+of+quantum+field+theory"} geometry of physics – A first idea of quantum field theory
              the section
              %em
                %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+A+first+idea+of+quantum+field+theory#Renormalization"} Renormalization
          %h2#definition Definition
          #FlowRenormalizationGroup.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization+group+flow"}> renormalization group flow
                )
            %p Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi vac
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mtext BV-BRST
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    vac
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    (E_{\text{BV-BRST}}, \mathbf{L}', \Delta_H )
            %p
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relativistic+field+theory"} relativistic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field+theory"} free
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum"} vacuum
              (according to
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "S-matrix#VacuumFree"} this def.
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interacting+field+theory"} interacting
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+QFT"} perturbative QFT
            %p
              Consider a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi RG
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} RG
              equipped with an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick+algebra"} Wick algebra
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/off-shell"} off-shell
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/microcausal+polynomial+observables"} microcausal polynomial observables
              with formal parameters adjoined (as in
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "S-matrix#FormalParameters"} this def.
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi rg
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi RG
                    %mo ×
                    %mi PolyObs
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mtext BV-BRST
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi mc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℏ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi PolyObs
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mtext BV-BRST
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi mc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℏ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ℏ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    rg_{(-)}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    RG \times PolyObs(E_{\text{BV-BRST}})_{mc}((\hbar))[ [ g, j ] ]
                    \\longrightarrow
                    PolyObs(E_{\text{BV-BRST}})_{mc}((\hbar))[ [ \hbar, g, j ] ]
                    \\,,
            %p
              hence for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi RG
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho \in RG
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+linear+map"} continuous linear map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi rg
                      %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} rg_\rho
              which has an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse"} inverse
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi rg
                      %mi ρ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi RG
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} rg_\rho^{-1} \in RG
              and is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              of the
              = succeed "-product" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick+algebra"} Wick algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star+product"} star product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \star_H
              induced by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wightman+propagator"} Wightman propagator
              of the given vauum
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi vac
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} vac
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi rg
                      %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mi H
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi rg
                      %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mi H
                    %msub
                      %mi rg
                      %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    rg_\rho( A_1 \star_H A_2 )
                    \\;=\;
                    rg_\rho(A_1) \star_H rg_\rho(A_2)
            %p such that the following conditions hold:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the action preserves the subspace of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/off-shell"} off-shell
                  polynomial
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+observables"} local observables
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/restriction"} restricts
                  as
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi rg
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi RG
                        %mo ×
                        %mi LocObs
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mtext BV-BRST
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi ℏ
                        %mo ,
                        %mi g
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %mi g
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi LocObs
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mtext BV-BRST
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi ℏ
                        %mo ,
                        %mi g
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %mi g
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        rg_{(-)}
                        \\;\colon\;
                        RG \times LocObs(E_{\text{BV-BRST}})[ [ \hbar, g, j ] ]\langle g,j\rangle
                        \\longrightarrow
                        LocObs(E_{\text{BV-BRST}})[ [ \hbar, g, j ] ]\langle g,j\rangle
              %li
                %p
                  the action respects the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+order"} causal order
                  of the spacetime support (
                  %a{:href => "A+first+idea+of+quantum+field+theory#SpacetimeSupport"}> this def.
                  ) of local observables, in that for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi O
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi O
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi LocObs
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mtext BV-BRST
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi ℏ
                        %mo ,
                        %mi g
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O_1, O_2 \in LocObs(E_{\text{BV-BRST}})[ [ \hbar, g, j] ]
                  we have
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mi supp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi O
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mrow
                            %mo ∨
                            %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                            %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                            %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                            %mo ∧
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi supp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi O
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo )
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mi supp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi rg
                            %mi ρ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi O
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mrow
                            %mo ∨
                            %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                            %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                            %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                            %mo ∧
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi supp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi rg
                            %mi ρ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi O
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\left(
                        supp(O_1)
                        \\,{\vee\!\!\!\wedge}\,
                        supp(O_2)
                        \\right)
                        \\phantom{A}
                        \\Rightarrow
                        \\phantom{A}
                        \\left(
                        supp(rg_\rho(O_1))
                        \\,{\vee\!\!\!\wedge}\,
                        supp(rg_\rho(O_2))
                        \\right)
                %p
                  for all
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ρ
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi RG
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho \in RG
            %p Then:
            %p
              The operation of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugation"} conjugation
              by this action on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observables"} observables
              induces an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-matrix"} S-matrix
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization+schemes"} renormalization schemes
              (
              %a{:href => "S-matrix#LagrangianFieldTheoryPerturbativeScattering"}> this def.
              ,
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "S-matrix#calSFunctionIsRenormalizationScheme"} this remark
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi LocObs
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mtext BV-BRST
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ℏ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi PolyObs
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mtext BV-BRST
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℏ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{S}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    LocObs(E_{\text{BV-BRST}})[ [ \hbar , g, j] ]
                    \\longrightarrow
                    PolyObs(E_{\text{BV-BRST}})( (\hbar) )[ [ g, j] ]
            %p
              a perturbative
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-matrix+scheme"} S-matrix scheme
              around the given
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field+theory"} free field
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum"} vacuum
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi vac
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} vac
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composite
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mi ρ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi rg
                      %mi ρ
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo ∘
                    %msubsup
                      %mi rg
                      %mi ρ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi LocObs
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mtext BV-BRST
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ℏ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi PolyObs
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mtext BV-BRST
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℏ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{S}^\rho
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    rg_\rho \circ \mathcal{S} \circ rg_{\rho}^{-1}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    LocObs(E_{\text{BV-BRST}})[ [ \hbar , g, j] ]
                    \\longrightarrow
                    PolyObs(E_{\text{BV-BRST}})( (\hbar) )[ [ g, j] ]
            %p
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-matrix"} S-matrix
              scheme, for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi RG
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho \in RG
            %p More generally, let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi vac
                      %mi ρ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mtext BV-BRST
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mi ρ
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    vac_\rho
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    (E_{\text{BV-BRST}}, \mathbf{L}'_\rho, \Delta_{H,\rho} )
            %p
              be a collection of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fixing"} gauge fixed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field+theory"} free field
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacua"} vacua
              parameterized by elements
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi RG
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho \in RG
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi rg
                      %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} rg_\rho
              as above, except that it is not an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism"} automorphism
              of any
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick+algebra"} Wick algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              between the
              = succeed "-structures" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick+algebra"} Wick algebra
            #eq:IntertwiningWickProductsActionRG.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi rg
                      %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                        %mo ,
                        %msup
                          %mi ρ
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %msub
                          %mi ρ
                          %mi vac
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi rg
                      %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi ρ
                          %mi vac
                    %msub
                      %mi rg
                      %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    rg_{\rho}( A_1 \star_{H, \rho^{-1} \rho_{vac}} A_2 )
                    \\;=\;
                    rg_{\rho}(A_1) \star_{H, \rho_{vac}} rg_{\rho}(A_2)
            %p
              for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mi vac
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi RG
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho, \rho_{vac} \in RG
            %p Then if
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mi ρ
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi ρ
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi RG
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{ \mathcal{S}_{\rho} \}_{\rho \in RG}
            %p
              is a collection of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-matrix+schemes"} S-matrix schemes
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fixing"} gauge fixed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field+theory"} free field
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacua"} vacua
              = succeed "," do
