                    \\mathcal{S}_{\rho_{vac}}
                    \\circ
                    \\mathcal{Z}_{\rho_{vac}}^{\rho_1 \rho_2}
                    \&amp; =
                    \\mathcal{S}_{\rho_{vac}}^{\rho_1 \rho_2 }
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\sigma_{\rho_1}
                    \\circ
                    \\underset{
                    \=
                    \\mathcal{S}_{\rho_1^{-1} \rho_{vac}}^{\rho_2}
                    \=
                    \\mathcal{S}_{\rho_1^{-1} \rho_{vac}}
                    \\circ
                    \\mathcal{Z}_{\rho_1^{-1} \rho_vac}^{\rho_2}
                    }{
                    \\underbrace{
                    \\sigma_{\rho_2}
                    \\circ
                    \\mathcal{S}_{\rho_2^{-1}\rho_1^{-1}\rho_{vac}}
                    \\circ
                    \\sigma_{\rho_2}^{-1}
                    }}
                    \\circ
                    \\sigma_{\rho_1}^{-1}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\underset{
                    \=
                    \\mathcal{S}_{\rho_{vac}}
                    \\circ
                    \\mathcal{Z}_{\rho_{vac}}^{\rho_1}
                    \\circ
                    \\sigma_{\rho_1}
                    }{
                    \\underbrace{
                    \\sigma_{\rho_1}
                    \\circ
                    \\mathcal{S}_{\rho_1^{-1} \rho_{vac}}
                    \\circ
                    \\overset{ = id }{
                    \\overbrace{
                    \\sigma_{\rho_1}^{-1}
                    \\circ
                    \\sigma_{\rho_1}
                    }
                    }
                    }}
                    \\circ
                    \\mathcal{Z}_{\rho_1^{-1} \rho_{vac}}^{\rho_2}
                    \\circ
                    \\sigma_{\rho_1}^{-1}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\mathcal{S}_{\rho_{vac}}
                    \\circ
                    \\mathcal{Z}_{\rho_{vac}}^{\rho_1}
                    \\circ
                    \\underbrace{
                    \\sigma_{\rho_1}
                    \\circ
                    \\mathcal{Z}_{\rho_1^{-1} \rho_{vac}}^{\rho_2}
                    \\circ
                    \\sigma_{\rho_1}^{-1}
                    }
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              This demonstrates the equation between vertex redefinitions to be shown after
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              with an S-matrix scheme. But by the uniqueness-clause in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/main+theorem+of+perturbative+renormalization"} main theorem of perturbative renormalization
              the composition operation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ρ
                          %mi vac
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}_{\rho_{vac}} \circ (-)
              as a function from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertex+redefinitions"} vertex redefinitions
              to S-matrix schemes is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+function"} injective
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#ScalingTransformationsRGFlow Scaling transformations
          %p
            We discuss (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RGFlowScalingTransformations"}
            below) that, if the field species involved have well-defined
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass+dimension"} mass dimension
            (example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ScalarFieldMassDimensionOnMinkowskiSpacetime"}
            below) then
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scaling+transformations"} scaling transformations
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            (example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ScalingTransformations"}
            below) induce a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization+group+flow"} renormalization group flow
            (def.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FlowRenormalizationGroup"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization+group+flows"} renormalization group flows
            (
            %a{:href => "#GellMannLow54"}> Gell-Mann&amp; Low 54
            ).
          #ScalingTransformations.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
