          %h2#references References
          %p
            The original informal discussion for RG-flow along
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scaling+transformations"} scaling transformations
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#GellMannLow54
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Murray+Gell-Mann"} Murray Gell-Mann
                and F. E. Low,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum Electrodynamics at Small Distances
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.fafnir.phyast.pitt.edu/py3765/GellManLow.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Callan70
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Curtis+Callan"}> Curtis Callan
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Broken Scale Invariance in Scalar Field Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.2.1541"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.2.1541
            %li#Symanzik70
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kurt+Symanzik"}> Kurt Symanzik
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Small distance behaviour in field theory and power counting
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01649434"} doi:10.1007/BF01649434
          %p
            Formulation in the rigorous context of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+perturbation+theory"} causal perturbation theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pAQFT"} pAQFT
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/main+theorem+of+perturbative+renormalization"} main theorem of perturbative renormalization
          %ul
            %li#BrunettiDuetschFredenhagen09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Romeo+Brunetti"}> Romeo Brunetti
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+D%C3%BCtsch"} Michael Dütsch
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaus+Fredenhagen"} Klaus Fredenhagen
              = succeed "," do
                %em Perturbative Algebraic Quantum Field Theory and the Renormalization Groups
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0901.2038"} arXiv:0901.2038
          %p reviewed in
          %ul
            %li#Duetsch18
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+D%C3%BCtsch"}> Michael Dütsch
              , section 3.5.3 of
